### 12.0.9 기존8소천체의 색·형태·참조 반지름 전수

RGB는설명용팔레트이며기존JPLradius/지도/좌표의대체원자료가아니다. Ceresresolved=true는기존Dawn지도가있음을반영하며다른7미분해표면과구분한다. null축비는측정구형이라는판정이아니다.

| ID·해상표면/지도보존 | 설명용RGB·정성근거·출처 | 형태·축비(a,b,c)·출처 | 형태 참조반지름 km·오차/정의·출처 | 개별 한계 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ceres · True/True | #888780 · illustrative_not_calibrated_RGB · Dawn resolved albedo/color maps exist; keep the adopted map, not this palette. · [원출처](https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.08550) | existing_resolved_map_preserved · 미기록 · 미기록 | 미기록 · 미기록 · 미기록 · 미기록 | RGB is a project display palette guided by qualitative observations, not calibrated true color. No random crater map, geographic texture, local ice distribution or current rotational phase is supplied. Unknown three-dimensional shape remains null; a display sphere is an explicit assumption. Literature size estimates and their assumptions do not replace existing JPL catalog radii or ephemerides. |
| haumea · False/False | #d8d8d2 · illustrative_not_calibrated_RGB · Visible geometric albedo 0.51 +/- 0.02 supports a bright display; the neutral RGB hue is unmeasured. · [원출처](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.03113) | published_occultation_lightcurve_triaxial_model · [1,0.7338501291989664,0.4418604651162791] · [원출처](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.03113) | 797.62 · {"minus_km":5.5,"plus_km":5.5} · Geometric mean of the adopted 1161/852/513 km semiaxes; nominal derived value, not an independent measurement. · [원출처](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.03113) | RGB is a project display palette guided by qualitative observations, not calibrated true color. No random crater map, geographic texture, local ice distribution or current rotational phase is supplied. Unknown three-dimensional shape remains null; a display sphere is an explicit assumption. Literature size estimates and their assumptions do not replace existing JPL catalog radii or ephemerides. The adopted triaxial model uses occultation plus light curve and neglects ring-light contribution; it is not a resolved shape mesh. The paper reports b uncertainty 4 km in its main text and 2 km in Methods; the factual snapshot retains both. The reported volume-equivalent diameter is 1595 +/- 11 km; ring-light alternatives change it, so the reference radius is model dependent. |
