| eris · False/False | #e4e3df · illustrative_not_calibrated_RGB · The occultation study gives visible geometric albedo about 0.96; the bright neutral palette is illustrative. · [원출처](https://www.eso.org/public/news/eso1142/) | unmeasured_3d_shape_display_sphere_assumed · 미기록 · 미기록 | 1163 · {"minus_km":6,"plus_km":6} · Half the 2010-occultation diameter 2326 +/- 12 km. · [원출처](https://www.eso.org/public/news/eso1142/) | RGB is a project display palette guided by qualitative observations, not calibrated true color. No random crater map, geographic texture, local ice distribution or current rotational phase is supplied. Unknown three-dimensional shape remains null; a display sphere is an explicit assumption. Literature size estimates and their assumptions do not replace existing JPL catalog radii or ephemerides. The occultation limb is close to spherical, but no resolved geographic surface or full axis solution is supplied. |
| sedna · False/False | #a55e49 · illustrative_not_calibrated_RGB · Sedna has an observed reddish color; this RGB shade is not a measured spectrum-to-color conversion. · [원출처](https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap040316.html) | unmeasured_3d_shape_display_sphere_assumed · 미기록 · 미기록 | 497.5 · {"minus_km":40,"plus_km":40} · Half the Herschel thermophysical diameter 995 +/- 80 km; not a resolved limb measurement. · [원출처](https://arxiv.org/abs/1204.0899) | RGB is a project display palette guided by qualitative observations, not calibrated true color. No random crater map, geographic texture, local ice distribution or current rotational phase is supplied. Unknown three-dimensional shape remains null; a display sphere is an explicit assumption. Literature size estimates and their assumptions do not replace existing JPL catalog radii or ephemerides. |
